The bug is in `db.js:11-16`: `withClient` calls `client.release()` only after `fn(client)` returns. If `fn` throws, the client is never released and leaks out of the pool permanently. Wrap it in try/finally:

```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    return await fn(client);
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}
```

Raising `max` would delay the timeouts but not stop the leak.

