The cause is in db.js:11-16 — `withClient` calls `client.release()` only after `fn(client)` succeeds:

```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  const result = await fn(client);
  client.release();
  return result;
}
```

If `fn(client)` throws, `release()` is skipped and that client is gone from the pool forever. Raising `max` just delays the same climb to a higher number.

Fix the leak with try/finally:

```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    return await fn(client);
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}
```

